WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.820
The Temple has become a place of trade.

2
00:00:02.870 --> 00:00:08.390
Jesus makes a whip of cords, drives out
the traders and overturns their tables.

3
00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:11.360
Yet the same Jesus
taught: love your enemies,

4
00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:13.200
and turn the other cheek.

5
00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:15.420
So is anger ever right?

6
00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:18.310
And can it ever justify violence?

7
00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:22.020
In this mission, you'll trace
violence back to Cain and Abel,

8
00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:24.820
and meet the idea of righteous anger.

9
00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:29.140
Then you'll read what Jesus taught in
Luke's Gospel about enemies and how to treat

10
00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:33.450
others, and weigh up whether
violence is ever justified.

11
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:37.880
Your mission: weigh up whether
anger can ever justify violence.
